@@ -3,3 +3,21 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value of `document` that the pointer refers to.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.js";
+
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": [10, 20] }, "/a~1b/1"); // 20
+resolvePointer({ a: 1 }, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+- The empty pointer refers to the whole document; `~0` and `~1` escape `~` and `/` (section 4).
+- It throws if the pointer is not valid (section 3), or does not resolve: missing member, array index
+  out of range, index with a leading zero or sign, the `-` token (nonexistent element past the end),
+  or stepping into a scalar.
+- Only own members are read, so `__proto__` or `constructor` never reach the prototype chain.
+  The document is not mutated. The URI fragment form (section 6) is not supported.
